      "id": 1,
      "text": "Temelec Hall, built in 1858 by Captain Granville P. Swift, a member of the historic Bear Flag Party.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temelec%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1936, Temelec Hall earned the title California Historical Landmark #237 for its 19th‑century heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://temelec.org/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The hall was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 2006, cementing its national significance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://temelec.org/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today, Temelec Hall serves as the core of the Temelec Adult Community Center, welcoming residents every day.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temelec%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community of Temelec sits on land that once formed the Temelec estate, including the hall, its coach‑house, and surrounding acreage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://temelec.org/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Temelec Hall also holds the distinction of being a Sonoma County Historic Landmark, honoring local history.",
